IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp4-overpayment`

-- Tests of sections 66 and 66.1. Every expected value is worked out by hand from the text, as written beside
-- the assertion. All amounts and dates are invented.

§ `Tests -- sections 66 and 66.1`


§§ `Section 66(1) and (2)`

-- A payment of 1000 to which the person is not entitled at all: return 1000.
#ASSERT `s 66(1) — the amount the person or estate must at once return` 1000 0 EQUALS 1000
-- A payment of 1000 where the entitlement is 600: return the excess, 400.
#ASSERT `s 66(1) — the amount the person or estate must at once return` 1000 600 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `s 66(1) — the amount the person or estate must at once return` 1000 1000 EQUALS 0
-- An underpayment is not a debt of the person's.
#ASSERT `s 66(1) — the amount the person or estate must at once return` 1000 1200 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 66(2) — the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable at any time` 1000 600 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(2) — the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable at any time` 1000 1000 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2) — the amount is a debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable at any time` 1000 1200 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.01) — the interest is a debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable at any time` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.01) — the interest is a debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable at any time` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.02) — the penalty is a debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable at any time` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.02) — the penalty is a debt due to Her Majesty, recoverable at any time` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Section 66(2.1) to (2.9) -- collecting the debt`

-- Indebtedness 500, 800 payable, no more than 300 without undue hardship: 300 now.
#ASSERT `s 66(2.1) — the most that may be deducted and retained out of an amount payable` 500 800 300 EQUALS 300
-- The hardship limit is above the debt: the whole debt, 500.
#ASSERT `s 66(2.1) — the most that may be deducted and retained out of an amount payable` 500 800 1000 EQUALS 500
-- Only 200 is payable to the person: 200.
#ASSERT `s 66(2.1) — the most that may be deducted and retained out of an amount payable` 500 200 1000 EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `s 66(2.1) — the most that may be deducted and retained out of an amount payable` 100 800 1000 EQUALS 100
-- Any deduction would cause undue hardship.
#ASSERT `s 66(2.1) — the most that may be deducted and retained out of an amount payable` 500 800 0 EQUALS 0
-- The Minister is of the opinion that the person is attempting to avoid payment: without delay, the day the opinion is formed.
#ASSERT `s 66(2.2) — the first day on which the Minister may certify the indebtedness that has not been recovered` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2021 3 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2021 5 5)
-- In any other case, once 30 days after the default (1 March 2021) have expired: 1 April 2021 (1 March plus 31 days).
#ASSERT `s 66(2.2) — the first day on which the Minister may certify the indebtedness that has not been recovered` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2021 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2021 3 1) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1)
#ASSERT `s 66(2.2) — the first day on which the Minister may certify the indebtedness that has not been recovered` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2021 5 5) (YearMonthDay 2020 12 31) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2021 1 31)
#ASSERT `s 66(2.3) — the registered certificate has the force and effect of a judgment of the Federal Court for a debt` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.3) — the registered certificate has the force and effect of a judgment of the Federal Court for a debt` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.4) — the certificate may also be registered in the superior court of a province` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.4) — the certificate may also be registered in the superior court of a province` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.5) — the costs and charges are recoverable as if certified and the certificate registered` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.5) — the costs and charges are recoverable as if certified and the certificate registered` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.6) — the document may be recorded to create security, a charge, lien or legal hypothec on the debtor's land` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.6) — the document may be recorded to create security, a charge, lien or legal hypothec on the debtor's land` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.6) — the document may be recorded to create security, a charge, lien or legal hypothec on the debtor's land` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.6) — the document may be recorded to create security, a charge, lien or legal hypothec on the debtor's land` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.7) — the person is required to pay the money otherwise payable to the debtor to the Receiver General` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.7) — the person is required to pay the money otherwise payable to the debtor to the Receiver General` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not served personally or by confirmed delivery service.
#ASSERT `s 66(2.7) — the person is required to pay the money otherwise payable to the debtor to the Receiver General` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.8) — the amount not paid as required by the notice is a debt due to Her Majesty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.8) — the amount not paid as required by the notice is a debt due to Her Majesty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.8) — the amount not paid as required by the notice is a debt due to Her Majesty` FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.9) — the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.9) — the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.9) — the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.9) — the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(2.9) — the affidavit is evidence of the personal service and of the request, notice or demand` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Section 66(3) to (6)`

-- Paragraph (a) alone: cannot be collected in the reasonably foreseeable future.
#ASSERT `s 66(3) — the Minister may remit all or any portion of the amount or excess` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Paragraph (b) alone: the cost of collecting would equal or exceed the amount.
#ASSERT `s 66(3) — the Minister may remit all or any portion of the amount or excess` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Paragraph (c) alone: undue hardship.
#ASSERT `s 66(3) — the Minister may remit all or any portion of the amount or excess` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Paragraph (d) alone: erroneous advice or administrative error.
#ASSERT `s 66(3) — the Minister may remit all or any portion of the amount or excess` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- None of the four.
#ASSERT `s 66(3) — the Minister may remit all or any portion of the amount or excess` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Convicted in connection with obtaining the payment: no power to remit, whatever the paragraphs.
#ASSERT `s 66(3) — the Minister may remit all or any portion of the amount or excess` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- No overpayment.
#ASSERT `s 66(3) — the Minister may remit all or any portion of the amount or excess` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Denied a benefit by administrative error.
#ASSERT `s 66(4) — the Minister must take remedial action to place the person in the position the person would be in` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Denied a division.
#ASSERT `s 66(4) — the Minister must take remedial action to place the person in the position the person would be in` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Denied an assignment.
#ASSERT `s 66(4) — the Minister must take remedial action to place the person in the position the person would be in` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(4) — the Minister must take remedial action to place the person in the position the person would be in` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The Minister is not satisfied that there was error.
#ASSERT `s 66(4) — the Minister must take remedial action to place the person in the position the person would be in` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(5) — the Minister must take remedial action, including attributing the earnings that would have been attributed` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 66(5) — the Minister must take remedial action, including attributing the earnings that would have been attributed` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- The agreement or order indicates there be no division.
#ASSERT `s 66(5) — the Minister must take remedial action, including attributing the earnings that would have been attributed` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Other criteria for a division are not met.
#ASSERT `s 66(5) — the Minister must take remedial action, including attributing the earnings that would have been attributed` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- It does not apply in relation to amounts owing under this Part.
#ASSERT `s 66(6) — section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act applies in relation to the amount` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(6) — section 155.1 of the Financial Administration Act applies in relation to the amount` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 66.1 -- request to cancel benefit`

-- An applicant for a disability benefit in receipt of a retirement pension, deemed disabled in the month the retirement pension first became payable: in or after.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(1.1) — subsection (1) does not apply to the cancellation of the retirement pension` `a retirement pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 6 20) (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Deemed disabled after the month.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(1.1) — subsection (1) does not apply to the cancellation of the retirement pension` `a retirement pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1) EQUALS TRUE
-- Deemed disabled before the month: not covered by the exception.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(1.1) — subsection (1) does not apply to the cancellation of the retirement pension` `a retirement pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 5 31) (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Not a retirement pension.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(1.1) — subsection (1) does not apply to the cancellation of the retirement pension` `a survivor's pension` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66.1(1.1) — subsection (1) does not apply to the cancellation of the retirement pension` `a retirement pension` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1) EQUALS FALSE
-- Payment commenced 15 January 2021; a written request on 15 January 2022, within 12 months after commencement.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(1) — the beneficiary may request cancellation of the benefit` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 1 15) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- One day later.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(1) — the beneficiary may request cancellation of the benefit` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 1 16) TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- On the day payment commenced.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(1) — the beneficiary may request cancellation of the benefit` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2021 1 15) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Before payment commenced.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(1) — the beneficiary may request cancellation of the benefit` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2021 1 14) TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Not in the prescribed manner.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(1) — the beneficiary may request cancellation of the benefit` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2021 6 1) FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Taken out by subsection (1.1).
#ASSERT `s 66.1(1) — the beneficiary may request cancellation of the benefit` (YearMonthDay 2021 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2021 6 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
-- Commenced 29 February 2020: 12 months later clamps to 28 February 2021 (NOTES.md fork register).
#ASSERT `s 66.1(1) — the beneficiary may request cancellation of the benefit` (YearMonthDay 2020 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2021 2 28) TRUE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Granted 10 June 2021; repaid 30 June 2022, within the 12 months following June 2021 (that is, by the end of June 2022).
#ASSERT `s 66.1(2) — the benefit is deemed for all purposes of this Act not to have been payable during the period` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2021 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2022 6 30) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- 1 July 2022: after the expiry.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(2) — the benefit is deemed for all purposes of this Act not to have been payable during the period` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2021 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2022 7 1) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Repaid before the request was granted: outside the period that begins on the granting.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(2) — the benefit is deemed for all purposes of this Act not to have been payable during the period` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2021 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2021 6 9) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- On the day it is granted.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(2) — the benefit is deemed for all purposes of this Act not to have been payable during the period` TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2021 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2021 6 10) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Under a provincial plan: the time provided under that plan governs, not the Act's 12 months.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(2) — the benefit is deemed for all purposes of this Act not to have been payable during the period` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
-- Under a provincial plan, repaid out of that plan's time.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(2) — the benefit is deemed for all purposes of this Act not to have been payable during the period` TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2021 6 15) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- The request was not granted.
#ASSERT `s 66.1(2) — the benefit is deemed for all purposes of this Act not to have been payable during the period` FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2021 6 10) (YearMonthDay 2021 6 15) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
